;; South Africa public holidays 2000-2040: external gold for ZA.
;; Regenerate: uv run --no-project --with holidays==0.109 python -I scripts/generate_mena_holiday_gold.py ZA
;; :days lists every holiday as (YEAR MONTH DAY NAME); any other day is not one.
(
 :country "ZA"
 :generated "2026-11-28"
 :from 2000 :to 2040
 :note "Public holidays of South Africa: Act 36 of 1994 Schedule 1 (from 1995) with the s. 2(1) Monday after a Sunday holiday (no further day when that Monday is a holiday), and every day the President declared under s. 2A 2000-2027 (Gazette proclamations: elections, Y2K, 2008-05-02, 27 Dec 2011/2016/2022, 2023-12-15, 2026-11-04), checked against the gov.za yearly lists. 2028-2040 are provisional: the Schedule and s. 2(1)."
 :weekends ((nil 6 7))
 :sources
 (
  (:title "Public Holidays Act 36 of 1994" :uri "https://www.gov.za/sites/default/files/gcis_document/201409/act36of1994.pdf"
   :text "Schedule 1: 12 public holidays — 1 Jan New Year's Day, 21 Mar Human Rights Day, Good Friday (Friday before Easter Sunday), Family Day (Monday after Easter Sunday), 27 Apr Freedom Day, 1 May Workers' Day, 16 Jun Youth Day, 9 Aug National Women's Day, 24 Sep Heritage Day, 16 Dec Day of Reconciliation, 25 Dec Christmas Day, 26 Dec Day of Goodwill. s. 2(1): a public holiday falling on a Sunday makes the following Monday a public holiday. s. 6: commencement 1 January 1995. Repeals the Public Holidays Act 5 of 1952.")
  (:title "Public Holidays Amendment Act 48 of 1995" :uri "https://www.gov.za/sites/default/files/gcis_document/201409/act48of1995.pdf"
   :text "Inserts s. 2A: 'The President may by proclamation in the Gazette declare any day to be a public holiday throughout the Republic or any part thereof'; widens the definition of 'public holidays' to include s. 2A days. Only amendment of Act 36/1994 listed on gov.za (no change to the Schedule or to s. 2(1)).")
